<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#national-redoubt-switzerland">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">National Redoubt (Switzerland)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1940">1940</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Réduit national</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The National Redoubt was the Swiss defence plan announced by General Henri Guisan in July 1940, after the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> left <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a> almost surrounded by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/axis-powers">Axis</a>. The army was to give up the populated lowlands and hold a fortified Alpine core, centred on the fortresses of Saint-Maurice, the Gotthard and Sargans, making an invasion costly and denying the vital Alpine passes.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/national-redoubt-switzerland.jpg" alt="National Redoubt (Switzerland)" width="320" height="207" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Auge=mit · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Reduit_Schweiz_Neu.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
